ue] [17592186397876 1084 #uuid "d97728d8-7183-59a2-bbab-433924b0cf9c" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397877 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397878 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397877 1069 "q-116499" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397877 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397877 1071 "![](images/1a/1a03b31de4f99e5e3ad4a65645beeeb067afc9fdfb0ccb39ada3aff305947f9d.png)\n\nThe length of the rectangular prism shown above is increasing at a rate of $7\\text{ in/min}.$ What is the rate of change of the surface area of the rectangular prism?" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397877 1072 #uuid "d6db5db2-50cf-5e89-b77b-4e40b77e862d" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397877 1074 "Let $x,y,z$ be the dimensions of the rectangular prism, and let $S$ be its surface area. The variables $x$ and $S$ change with time. In particular, we are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =8\\text{ in}, \\\\ z & =12\\text{ in}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =7\\text{ in}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nWe want to find the rate of change of $S$ knowing the rate of change of $x.$ So, we start with the formula for the surface area of the rectangular prism:\n\n$$\nS=2xz+2xy+2yz\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known values, we get\n\n$$\nS=2(12)(x)+2x(8)+2(12)(8)=40x+192.\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =40(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the above expression using $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=7,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =40(7)=280{\\text{ in}}^{2}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rectangular prism's surface area is increasing at a rate of $280\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{min}.$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397878 1075 #edb/re