\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5{x}^{4}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}+Cx+D \\\\  & ={x}^{5}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397934 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397935 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397934 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397936 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397934 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397937 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397934 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397938 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397934 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397939 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397934 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397934 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397934 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397937 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397934 1080 #uuid "7d7d8f65-a93b-5daa-b8fa-34a0b4f4a5ba" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397935 1081 "y={x}^{5}+C{x}^{2}+Dx" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397935 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397935 1084 #uuid "2339eddd-c520-53fc-835c-406bf5642b8b" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397936 1081 "y=4{x}^{4}+C{x}^{2}+Dx" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397936 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397936 1084 #uuid "6cfc929f-0e67-5e47-80b6-d2949d1be4b0" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397937 1081 "y={x}^{5}+Cx+D" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397937 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397937 1084 #uuid "4dd5ffc9-d74f-592b-a383-53ba3803f136" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397938 1081 "y=4{x}^{5}+Cx+D" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397938 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397938 1084 #uuid "395e4984-cf1d-534b-b01f-09b03aa00ba5" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397939 1081 "y=5{x}^{4}+Cx+D" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397939 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397939 1084 #uuid "796c5808-234b-5385-a5e5-513d3b55563c" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397940 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397941 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397940 1069 "q-120844" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397940 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397940 1071 "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}},$ where $t>0$ is the time in seconds. If the particle has velocity $v=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=4\\,\\text{s},$  determine the moment in time when the particle is stationary." 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397940 1072 #uuid "0588ded7-d4bd-5616-b35b-33100943aa76" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397940 1074 "The particle is stationary when $v=0\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.$\n\nFirst, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int -\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{t}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $v(4)=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & =\\frac{4}{(4)}+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & =1+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=\\frac{4}{t}-\\frac{2}{3}.$\n\nNow, we find the moments in time when $v=0\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{t}-\\frac{2}{3} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{t} & =\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ t & =\\frac{12}{2} \\\\ t & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particle is stationary when $t=6\\,\\text{s}.$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397941 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397942 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397941 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397943 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397941 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397944 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397941 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397945 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397941 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397946 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397941 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397941 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397941 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397945 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397941 1080 #uuid "695e7fd0-433d-51f0-b01d-00b9f5bc61a3" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397942 1081 "t=3\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397942 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397942 1084 #uuid "602aa483-d67f-5404-8467-f27f01940f90" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397943 1081 "t=4\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397943 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397943 1084 #uuid "14d09f20-c9c1-5eab-bc98-c123faf3e1b4" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397944 1081 "t=0\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397944 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397944 1084 #uuid "dbad500b-d968-57c7-8690-6808ade1af6f" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397945 1081 "t=6\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397945 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397945 1084 #uuid "427f7f46-348f-5d5b-8214-11acace487f2" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397946 1081 "t=2\\,\\text{s}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397946 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397946 1084 #uuid "5f5d956d-a3db-5f17-a60a-c65874e02299" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397947 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397948 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397947 1069 "q-120911" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397947 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397947 1071 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x\\sqrt{y},\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUse Euler's method with three steps of equal size to approximate $y(3).$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397947 1072 #uuid "13b68e5e-22d6-5fa0-a4a4-6c5d1f4c0a70" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397947 1074 "First, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(3).$ The distance from $x=0$ and $x=3$ is $3,$ and since we are asked to use three steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-0}{3}=\\frac{3}{3}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with Euler's method. We'll start by creating a table that includes the initial condition data $y(0)=1.$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 1.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the first row) and the values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x\\sqrt{y}=0\\cdot 1=0 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=0\\cdot 1=0 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+1=1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+0=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 2.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x\\sqrt{y}=1\\cdot \\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=1\\cdot 1=1 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=2+1=2 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+1=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $2$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 3.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the third row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x\\sqrt{y}=2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1=2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=2+1=3 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=2+2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $2$ | $2\\sqrt{2}$ | $2\\sqrt{2}$ |\n| $3$ | $2+2\\sqrt{2}$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(3)≈2+2\\sqrt{2}.$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397948 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397949 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397948 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397950 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397948 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397951 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397948 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397952 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397948 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397953 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397948 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397948 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397948 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397950 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397948 1080 #uuid "34d0bc62-23d7-51e0-a40e-82b353c65411" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397949 1081 "4\\sqrt{2}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397949 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397949 1084 #uuid "111eb72f-77db-56c0-809e-6b4a599df81c" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397950 1081 "2+2\\sqrt{2}" 131941