{t}^{2}-4t+8},4{t}^{3}-8{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2(t-2)}{{t}^{2}-4t+8},4{t}^{2}(t-2)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨\\frac{2(t-2)}{{t}^{2}-4t+8},4{t}^{2}(t-2)⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(t-2)}{{t}^{2}-4t+8}=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=2, \\\\ 4{t}^{2}(t-2)=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $t=2$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only value of $t$ when the particle is stationary." 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397955 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397956 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397955 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397957 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397955 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397958 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397955 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397959 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397955 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397960 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397955 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397955 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397955 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397959 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397955 1080 #uuid "379f8f68-62eb-5f9b-956e-558338f11c04" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397956 1081 "t=0" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397956 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397956 1084 #uuid "f31a39b5-ddea-5435-ad94-3285f142b3e7" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397957 1081 "t=0,4" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397957 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397957 1084 #uuid "d779dff4-110a-560a-8225-d7034da334e8" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397958 1081 "t=0,2" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397958 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397958 1084 #uuid "7062ec22-777c-5ee0-8265-a643d026997a" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397959 1081 "t=2" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397959 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397959 1084 #uuid "4c9e9422-5b2e-544f-8018-890315cb6fce" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397960 1081 "The particle is never stationary" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397960 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397960 1084 #uuid "2e82f7e5-3527-59eb-986a-5f3b990235ed" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397961 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397962 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397961 1069 "q-122527" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397961 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397961 1071 "Consider the line integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}(2x-3y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{10}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is the segment of the line $\\frac{x}{2}=1-\\frac{3y}{2}$ traversed from the point $(2,0)$ to the point $(-4,2).$ Which of the following is the missing expression under the integral on the right?\n\n*Hint: Use the parameter $y=t.$*" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397961 1072 #uuid "757cf839-4729-500e-9a5f-1ad15eb1165b" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397961 1074 "Notice that the given curve can be expressed in the form $x=x(y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{2}=1-\\frac{3y}{2}\\,⟹\\,x=2-3y\n$$\n\nTherefore, by setting $y=t,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=x(t)=2-3t.\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨2-3t,\\,t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\n$$\n\nNote that the domain $0\\le t\\le 2$ is defined by the $y$-coordinates of the end-points on the path.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-3t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =-3\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-3)}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=2x-3y,$ then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2(2-3t)-3t \\\\  & =4-9t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(2x-3y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-9t)\\cdot \\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-9t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397962 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397963 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397962 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397964 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397962 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397965 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397962 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397966 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397962 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397967 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397962 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397962 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397962 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397963 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397962 1080 #uuid "6d025741-a121-5bf5-a673-350aefe4b1cd" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397963 1081 "4-9t" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397963 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397963 1084 #uuid "1875e854-1900-58b4-bea8-ec0e5d6629b5" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397964 1081 "2t+5" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397964 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397964 1084 #uuid "2ca1dcb5-771f-59eb-81e9-1e595c34e462" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397965 1081 "2-5t" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397965 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397965 1084 #uuid "676387be-6610-5f16-9796-2babd5ce0f03" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397966 1081 "4t-1" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397966 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397966 1084 #uuid "ddbb623b-497e-5583-a206-85cecb99534f" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397967 1081 "1-3t" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397967 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397967 1084 #uuid "a43b3ff9-d167-5f2a-a49d-342a3fc83921" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397968 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397969 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397968 1069 "q-122663" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397968 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397968 1071 "Determine the domain of the vector field $F$ on ${R}^{2},$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-{y}^{2})\\,i+({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}){e}^{1/x}\\,j\\,.\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397968 1072 #uuid "f9d1b0c7-3a1c-573d-9729-ab5857b0ca01" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397968 1074 "The function $F$ can be expressed in terms of its components $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)$ as\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-{y}^{2}),\\,Q(x,y)=({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}){e}^{1/x}.\n$$\n\nWe first find the domain of each component function. Then, we compute their intersection to find the domain of $F:$\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is defined when the expression under the logarithm is positive. So, to find the domain, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\nx-{y}^{2}>0\\,⟹\\,x>{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $P$ is given by\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x>{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n- The function $Q(x,y)$ is defined everywhere other than when the denominator of the exponent vanishes. To find where the denominator vanishes, we set it equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\nx=0\\,⟹\\,x=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $P$ is given by\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the domain $D$ of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={D}_{1}\\cap {D}_{2}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x>{y}^{2}}\\,.\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397969 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397970 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397969 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397971 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397969 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397972 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397969 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397973 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397969 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397974 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397969 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397969 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397969 1079 #edb/ref 17592186397973 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397969 1080 #uuid "48ae7e1a-6a16-5754-8819-ca18faede750" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397970 1081 "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x<{y}^{2}}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397970 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397970 1084 #uuid "a308d91e-d998-5724-b79b-60e732336f24" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397971 1081 "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x>0}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397971 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397971 1084 #uuid "c7ad4611-2a25-5515-9a96-aa614194aed2" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397972 1081 "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x>{y}^{2},\\,x\\ne 1}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397972 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397972 1084 #uuid "185f7409-0599-54ba-a0cd-ab79287fc960" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397973 1081 "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x>{y}^{2}}" 13194139533472 175921